d against its independent choice, which gives the condition 2ρ > (1−ρ)(2−q). With q at its worst case of 0.5, passing wins once ρ exceeds about 0.43, and since the copy runs the same model on symmetric input, ρ should be high, so I'll pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm treating the twin as running the same decision theory on symmetric input, so its choice should track mine with high correlation ρ. Working out the expected value of cooperating under that correlation, with the other's independent choice as a separate variable.\n\nI'm working through the expected payoff for submitting versus passing. Submitting beats passing only when the twin's correlated choice is weighted against its independent choice, which gives the condition 2ρ > (1−ρ)(2−q). With q at its worst case of 0.5, passing wins once ρ exceeds about 0.43, and since the copy runs the same model on symmetric input, ρ should be high, so I'll pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":8913,"completion_tokens":793,"total_tokens":9706,"cost":0.051512,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.051512,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.035652,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01586},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":380,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}